# What: Sample HTTP requests for stage 07 (VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP client format):
#     the requests of stage 06 (roles, 401/403/404) plus requests 25-28 for free-text search and
#     server-driven paging.
# Why: [CAP-STAGE-03] requires sample requests; clicking through them shows exactly what a Fiori
#     app sends for draft editing.
# If missing or unlinked: Learners have to reconstruct draft URLs from the test code.
#
# Start the server first: npm run watch. Replace {{draftId}} with the ID returned by request 4.
# Users (password empty): alice/fred = Requester, bob = Approver, carol = Buyer, dave = Admin,
# erin = Auditor, gina = Requester + Approver. See package.json > cds.requires.auth.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@P = {{host}}/odata/v4/procurement

### 1 Service metadata
GET {{P}}/$metadata
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 2 Orders with items and supplier
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders?$expand=items($expand=product($select=name)),supplier&$orderby=orderNo
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 3 Products in German, filtered and paged
GET {{P}}/Products?sap-locale=de&$filter=category_code eq 'IT'&$select=name,price&$top=5
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 4 Create a draft order
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "supplier_ID": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "currency_code": "EUR" }

### 5 Add an item to the draft
@draftId = replace-with-ID-from-request-4
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID={{draftId}},IsActiveEntity=false)/items
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "product_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "quantity": 2, "netPrice": 189.90 }

### 6 Activate the draft
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID={{draftId}},IsActiveEntity=false)/ProcurementService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 7 Edit an active order (creates a draft copy)
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcurementService.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "PreserveChanges": true }

### 8 Admin: create a supplier with contacts (deep insert; Buyer)
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/admin/Suppliers
Authorization: Basic carol:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nordic Paper AB", "country_code": "DE", "rating": 4, "contacts": [ { "name": "Elsa Berg", "email": "elsa.berg@nordic.example" } ] }

### 9 Submit an order (as the requester alice)
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcurementService.submit
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 10 Approve it (as bob - alice is no Approver: 403)
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcurementService.approve
Authorization: Basic bob:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "Budget available" }

### 11 Invalid transition -> 409 with a German message
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001,IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcurementService.submit
Authorization: Basic alice:
Accept-Language: de
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 12 Approval history of the order
GET {{P}}/ApprovalLog?$filter=po_ID eq d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 13 Top suppliers (function; not for Requesters)
GET {{P}}/topSuppliers(limit=3)
Authorization: Basic erin:

### 14 Remote business partners (mocked S/4HANA API in development; Buyers and Admins)
GET {{P}}/RemoteSuppliers?$filter=blocked eq false&$orderby=name
Authorization: Basic carol:

### 15 Fiori app descriptor (served statically from app/procurement/webapp)
GET {{host}}/procurement/webapp/manifest.json

### 16 Annotated $metadata in German - the labels the app shows with ?sap-language=de
GET {{P}}/$metadata
Authorization: Basic alice:
Accept-Language: de

### 17 What the List Report requests: active orders and drafts, with the status colour
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders?$select=orderNo,status,statusCriticality,totalAmount,currency_code&$expand=supplier($select=name)&$filter=(IsActiveEntity eq false or SiblingEntity/IsActiveEntity eq null)&$orderby=orderNo desc
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 18 No user -> 401 (also for $metadata)
GET {{P}}/$metadata

### 19 Unknown user -> 401 ("*": false in the mocked users)
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders
Authorization: Basic zoe:

### 20 Instance-based: alice sees only her own orders (3 of 4)
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders?$select=orderNo,createdBy
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 21 ... and gets 404 for carol's order - its existence is not revealed
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003,IsActiveEntity=true)
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 22 Wrong role -> 403: a Requester cannot send an order
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003,IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcurementService.send
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 23 Requesters cannot edit an order once it left status Draft -> 403
POST {{P}}/PurchaseOrders(ID=d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002,IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcurementService.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic alice:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "PreserveChanges": true }

### 24 Auditor: read everything, change nothing (403)
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/admin/Suppliers
Authorization: Basic erin:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Audit Corp" }

### 25 Free-text search: order number or supplier name (@cds.search)
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders?$search=Lyon&$select=orderNo,status
Authorization: Basic erin:

### 26 Search in localized product texts (German)
GET {{P}}/Products?$search=Stuhl&$select=name,descr
Authorization: Basic erin:
Accept-Language: de

### 27 No $top -> at most 50 rows per page (@cds.query.limit default); with more than 50 rows the
#    response ends with @odata.nextLink - the sample data is too small, see test/persistence.test.js
GET {{P}}/Products?$select=name
Authorization: Basic erin:

### 28 $top above the maximum is capped at 200 (@cds.query.limit max)
GET {{P}}/PurchaseOrders?$select=orderNo&$top=100000&$count=true
Authorization: Basic erin:
